title The half that drives and the half that describes
prompt The autonomous loop's own baton -- take the next agent-doable lap, reds first, Lindy-first crux-first, and grade what you touch.
think The cold open reddened on seed_link before I had chosen any work, so the work chose itself.
think The scan named its own cure in its refusal line -- name the withheld room in prose instead -- and taking a tool's own prescribed repair is cheaper than inventing a second one.
think The interesting question was never the link. It was why a room reclassified on Keaton's word an hour earlier was still withheld, and the answer was one missing line in the file's driver half.
think I nearly shipped a wrong reason. My first reading said `keaton@dc1` matched no scrub rule; running the scrub over the room showed it becoming `the-maintainer@dc1`, and the one string that actually survives is `vultr`.
obs A MANIFEST WITH TWO HALVES CAN DISAGREE, AND ONLY ONE HALF IS READ BY THE MACHINE. `template-manifest.bron` carries `allow` lines that drive `tools/fixtures/s/sow_project.sh` and `template|scrub|personal` lines its own header calls intent documentation. The `20260909` reclassification of `nixos` from personal to template landed in the intent half alone, so the room reads as shipping to every human eye and ships nothing.
obs THE GUARD THAT CAUGHT IT WAS LOOKING SOMEWHERE ELSE. `seed_link` reads whether a shipped document links into a room the seed lacks. It reddened because `SOURCE.md` gained a pointer saying *which ships with this seed*. Nothing in the tree reads the manifest's two halves against each other; that disagreement was invisible until a sentence depended on it.
obs THE INCENSE LAP'S OWN LOG RECORDS THE MECHANISM OF THE MISS. It tried `allow nixos`, `sow_personal_scan` refused it because `personal nixos` stood, the row was reclassified to `template` to clear the refusal -- and the `allow` line was never written back. A refusal answered by editing the other half is how a decision ends up recorded in the half nobody executes.
obs MEASURE THE OUTPUT, NEVER THE RULES. Reading `sow_scrub.sed` I concluded `keaton@dc1` survives, since `s/Keaton/` is case-sensitive. Running the scrub proved a lowercase rule exists and the address falls. The one string that survives is `vultr`, matched case-insensitively by `sow_leak_scan.sh`'s `Vultr`, so adding the allow line today would refuse the publish rather than leak. The wall holds; the order is what is missing.
obs NINE ROOTS CARRY A SHIP-INTENT VERDICT AND NO ALLOW LINE, and most are honest. Five are the documented file-by-file hold, `template-manifest.bron` says withheld anyway, `vendor` is submodules. Only `kyri` and `nixos` carry no note, which is the shape a meter would separate from a habit.
obs AGAINST MYSELF, THE SAME FAULT MY ELDER BLOCK RECORDS. I edited SOURCE.md and a rule while the cold pass was still running, so its close digest disagrees with its open and it reads tree_moved. One lap old and repeated.
